    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Reintroduce Regina-REXX, an ANSI-compliant REXX interpreter.

Resubmission of request 1371181, which was declined for a file conflict
with ooRexx 5.2. That conflict is now gone: ooRexx in Factory has since
migrated to libalternatives (request 1371842, accepted 2026-08-19) and
ships /usr/bin/rexx and /usr/bin/rxqueue as plain symlinks to alts, the
same form this package uses.

The sources are unchanged from the declined request.

Verified rather than assumed: the two packages share exactly five paths -
/usr/bin/rexx, /usr/bin/rxqueue and three libalternatives directories.
Both symlinks are lrwxrwxrwx root:root pointing at alts in both packages,
so rpm permits both to own them, with the config files at different
priorities (Regina-REXX 15, ooRexx 20). Installing Regina-REXX,
libregina3, ooRexx and liboorexx4 in a single rpm transaction completes
with no conflict.

Local build green, rpmlint 0 errors.</comment>
